> The checks of category range are horribly inconsistent here ... and they should all be the same.

Actually I looked further at this. The checks are consistent already. Where we have code that looks like this:

```
    category = ossl_trace_get_category(category);
    if (category < 0)
        return NULL;
````
The full range check is included as part of `ossl_trace_get_category()`. If it is out of the range (`category < 0 || category >= OSSL_TRACE_CATEGORY_NUM`) then the return value from `ossl_trace_get_category()` is always -1, so a check of `category < 0` is sufficient, and anything more would be redundant.

The only thing missing here is a check for `category < 0` in `OSSL_trace_end()`
